e":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nTested on Godot 4.5.1 RC2.\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 10\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen dragging/dropping a GLTF file with an associated .bin file in the Godot file explorer, only the GLTF file is moved. The .bin file remains in its original location, causing the resource to break. If I manually move the bin file afterward, the resource is still broken until I delete the corresponding .import files.\n\nThis behavior also happens for OBJ files with associated .mtl files, and possibly for other file types with dependencies. It would greatly improve usability if, when moving files in the editor, all related/dependent files (such as .bin and .mtl) are moved together.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create or import a GLTF file with an associated .bin file into a Godot project.\n2. Drag and drop the GLTF file to a different directory in the Godot editor's file explorer.\n3. Observe that only the GLTF file is moved; the .bin file remains in the original directory.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[bin-files.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22871243/bin-files.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_